#X obj 704 8 radio;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 276 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A non-GUI radio switch. When an index is received on
the inlet \, the corresponding outlet is set to 1 and all the others
are set to 0\. This is the control-level equivalent of the [hradio]
GUI object.;
#X text 240 153 Typical use cases: switching between exclusive processing
modes (reverb / delay / dry) \, selecting one active preset bank \,
multiplexing one of several control or audio streams \, routing a signal
to one of several channels \, driving a simple state machine (record
/ play / stop) \, gating events \, or triggering different algorithms
depending on the selected mode.;
#X text 240 269 Note: [radio] is designed for cases where exactly one
option must be active at a time. If several states should be active
simultaneously \, use regular [toggle] or [select] objects instead.;
